(e) touching-state chain
    return probability r = 0.666666666667 (claim 2/3); E[N_touch] = 1/(1-r) = 3.0000000000 (claim 3)
    simulated P(A-walk from 1 hits 0) = 0.5008 (claim 1/2; truncation at level 200)
    kappa = E[Bayes loss of one touching step] = 0.7995167363 bits
    E[L_P*(infinity)] = 3 kappa = 2.3985502090 bits
    simulated (2000 runs, n=200): E[N_touch] = 2.9250 +- 0.0544; P(N_touch=j) for j=1..5: [0.355, 0.2155, 0.14, 0.0935, 0.0685] (geometric(1/3): [0.3333, 0.2222, 0.1481, 0.0988, 0.0658])
    simulated E[L_P*(200)] = 2.3390 +- 0.0607 (claim 2.3986)

